<!--
  The Mac agent speaks plain HTTP. That is deliberate: it is only reachable
  over Tailscale, which already wraps everything in WireGuard, so adding TLS
  would mean managing certificates for a link that is not cleartext on the
  wire anyway. Android blocks cleartext by default from API 28, and this
  config re-allows it.

  It is allowed GLOBALLY rather than per-domain because the agent is dialled
  by whatever the user typed (usually a bare 100.x.y.z tailnet IP) and
  this config cannot express "any address in 100.64.0.0/10". The app makes
  no other network request today (see AndroidManifest.xml). When the exec
  slice lands it brings its own token; that is the point to revisit this.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
